hi everyone sal khan here and i just  wanted to  tell y'all that we've reached kind of  several really cool milestones at khan  lab school which you can learn more  about it  connlabschool.org or kls.org  a lot of folks are surprised to hear  that i started a physical school back in  2014 when i'm so associated with online  learning but i've never viewed online as  somehow a replacement for an in-person  experience the dream has always been  that online can unlock the physical  experience it can allow students to  learn at a pace that is appropriate for  them it could allow for mastery-based  learning where if you get an eighty  percent on something you don't just get  a c on your forehead and your permanent  transcript and then you're expected to  learn the next concept that builds on  that 20 gap instead you're expected to  master the concept so you always have a  strong foundation  that we can unlock a situation where  when human beings get to a classroom  together both the students and the  teachers they're able to interact with  each other they're able to collaborate  with each other they're able to have  socratic dialogues have games they're  able to  do projects together we wanted to create  a reality where students aren't just  accountable for their own  gains or their own progress but also for  each other that they're invested in each  other that they are unusually  collaborative  we wanted to explore blurring the lines  between high school and college if kids  are able to learn more be truly curious  be truly engaged why can't they learn  faster than you would normally expect  the middle schoolers can learn high  school concepts  high school students can learn college  concepts and get credit for it so that  by the time they graduate they're  already operating at a junior or senior  level in college and actually getting  credit for it and so  the milestone that we're at is that  we're actually now at a full k-12 school  over 200 students we have our first  graduates this year and you can imagine  in the early days a lot of people  weren't well these are all interesting  ideas sal but will this work and it's a  lab school there's all sorts of stuff  that we're constantly trying but you  know when i look at this year's  graduating cohort i'm incredibly proud  of them  mainly for who they have become as human  beings but some of the traditional  metrics by which we measure students  they're also  crushing it i guess this is the best way  to say it which is which is a which is  really powerful to show that you can  create a learning experience where kids  are intrinsically curious they're  intrinsically want to collaborate with  each other and just want to learn more  but as a byproduct of it not as a goal  of it they're able to do incredibly well  on standardized tests our students are  scoring  on average better on standardized tests  than some of the very top universities  in in the country or in the world  they are getting into some of the top uh  universities in the world  even though they don't have traditional  letter grades because the universities  are seeing that the grades of  mastery-based learning are even more  powerful because it's a higher standard  it's expecting that all students really  mastered the concepts we're deepening  our partnership with foothill college  which is a local college in the area to  get the best of both worlds the high  school experience and the college  experience and so we have some exciting  things that i can't announce just yet  also on the capacity side and so that's  why i'm out here telling folks normally  we can only admit a few folks every year  but this year there might be an  opportunity for more so if you're  interested if you live in the san  francisco bay area in particular within  driving distance to mountain view palo  alto los altos  encourage you to take a look at it and  i'm happy to answer any questions in the  message board below that you might have  about khan lab school  my kids go there i teach there i work  very closely with the faculty and the  administration there  and what's exciting about it for me is  that not just creating a really unique  learning experience for  the students who attend but as a lab  school creating a model that can be  replicated throughout the world so once  again happy to answer any questions that  anyone might have
 

